# Family A11: the Kafka client library (drivers/kafka = franz-go against
# drivers/kafka/kafkago = segmentio/kafka-go). See hack/bakeoff.sh.
#
# the benchmark configuration row A11's arms are two CLIENT LIBRARIES in two modules,
# which is the one shape `hack/bakeoff.sh` could not express: it runs one
# `go test` in one package, and §9.4 step 2 wants the arms interleaved inside
# one invocation. The two can only be in one package if that package imports
# both drivers, and the only one in this repository that does is the kafka-go
# driver's own test binary -- it already imports drivers/kafka for the
# cross-driver equivalence suite and for kfake.
#
# Measuring both arms in one binary is also what makes the comparison honest
# in the way that matters most: one process, one broker instance, one Go
# runtime and one GOMAXPROCS for both arms. Two runs in two processes would
# differ by whatever else the host did between them.
MODDIR=drivers/kafka/kafkago
PKG=.
BENCH=BenchmarkKafkaClient
REF=franz
AUTO_KEY=kafka_client
KINDS_TEST=TestKafkaClientKindsList
# Nothing binds to this family's winner: which Kafka client library is
# canonical is ADR-013's decision and not an `Auto` constant, exactly as
# family A10's unsafe build is not one. §9.1 row A11 ends "loser demoted to
# community", which is a statement about the driver's TIER (§7.1) and about
# the driver page, not about a generated binding.
AUTO_FILE=-
ADR=13
TITLE="Kafka client library: franz-go against segmentio/kafka-go (A11)"

#
# CRITERION is the benchmark configuration's decision column for this row, quoted.
# MATRIX is the IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX grid the campaign measures the family at.
# DECIDED_AT names the benchmark-name segments the criterion is read at, and
# DECIDED_ON the metrics; `make bench-lint` lists the family's benchmarks at
# the declared grid and fails when a term or a metric is missing from the rows
# every kind has in common, which is the only data `bakeoff decide` reads.
CRITERION="throughput & p99 within budget, rebalance correctness -> franz-go expected; loser demoted to community"
# MATRIX=default is the only grid: §9.1 row A11 states its own sweep inside
# the benchmark name -- four operations at three payload sizes -- and the
# benchmark has no IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX branch, so there is no wider grid to ask
# for.
MATRIX=default
DECIDED_AT="publish batch consume endtoend 64B 1KiB 64KiB"
DECIDED_ON="ns/op allocs/op B/op msgs/s"
# What this family's measurement cannot produce, and where the evidence for it
# lives instead. §9.1 row A11 asks for four things beyond ns/op, and three of
# them are not benchmark metrics at all.
#
# The broker is an in-process kfake cluster and not the container the row
# names. That is deliberate for the ns/op half -- a container's broker cost is
# common-mode and both arms pay it identically, so it adds variance to the
# difference without adding information -- and it is a real gap for the p99
# half, where a container's fsync and replication are part of the latency the
# row wants bounded. `make bench-lint` lists every family's rows at
# -benchtime=1x on every `make ci`, so a family whose rows needed Docker would
# either start containers in every agent's CI run or select no benchmark at
# all.
# NB: entries are separated by ";" and nothing inside an entry may contain one,
# or the parser reads the fragment after it as a key with no text -- which is
# what `make bench-lint` refused on the first draft of this file.
CRITERION_GAP="p99-ns=the broker is an in-process kfake cluster and not the container the benchmark configuration row A11 names, so the container latency comes from BenchmarkDriver in each driver module with IQMQ_KAFKA_ADDR set (assumption B05.18); rebalance-correctness=a correctness gate rather than a metric, established by the five critical scenarios of drivers/kafka/critical_test.go and drivers/kafka/kafkago/critical_test.go, whose first scenario the two drivers answer differently (assumption B05.5); rebalance-storm=not measured by this family, and the eager-versus-cooperative difference it would expose is established by TestCriticalRebalanceWithDeliveriesInFlight in both driver modules; reconnect-chaos=not measured by this family, and conformance/chaos plus each driver own leader-change scenario are where it lives"
